# Environment Variables

Copy this to `.env` and fill in your values.

```
# Database
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/jokai"

# Discord Bot
DISCORD_TOKEN="your-bot-token"
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID="your-client-id"
GUILD_ID="your-test-server-id"

# Encryption
ENCRYPTION_KEY="your-secret-key-min-32-characters-long"

# OAuth (for website admin login)
DISCORD_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID="your-oauth-client-id"
DISCORD_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET="your-oauth-secret"
DISCORD_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI="http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/discord"

# Website
NEXT_PUBLIC_BOT_INVITE_URL="https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=YOUR_ID&scope=bot&permissions=PERMS"
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# File Storage (for proofs and screenshots)
STORAGE_PATH="/var/jokai/uploads"

# Monitoring
HEALTHCHECK_URL="https://hc-ping.com/your-id"

# Environment
NODE_ENV="development"
```

**In production (.env.production):**
- Use proper DATABASE_URL pointing to your PostgreSQL instance
- Set NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL to your domain (e.g., https://jokai.example.com)
- Set DISCORD_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI to your production URL
- Never commit secrets to git
